    "result_text": "I implemented `build_client` in `app/llm_client.py`, and it meets all four ops requirements. `pytest -q` passes (1 test), and I also ran a separate check with a stub transport.\n\n**Implementation:**\n- **Timeouts:** `Timeout(30.0, connect=5.0)` gives connect=5, read=30, write=30, pool=30. It's set on both the HTTP client and the `OpenAI` client, because the SDK sends its own timeout with every request and would otherwise ignore the HTTP client's setting.\n- **Retries:** `max_retries=2`.\n- **Logging:** a request event hook on the HTTP client logs `\"%s %s\"` (method, URL) at INFO on `app.http`. The hook runs on every send, so each retry gets its own log line.\n- **Transport:** passed straight through to the HTTP client. When it's `None`, the client's default transport is used.\n- I used `openai.DefaultHttpxClient` rather than a bare HTTP client so the SDK's default connection limits and redirect behaviour stay in place.\n\n**Check:** I used a stub transport that always returns HTTP 500. The effective timeout was `Timeout(connect=5.0, read=30.0, write=30.0, pool=30.0)` and `max_retries` was 2. The stub received 3 calls (1 attempt plus 2 retries), and `app.http` logged `GET https://api.openai.com/v1/models` three times before the call raised `InternalServerError`.\n\n**Things to know:**\n- **Context7 was unavailable:** it returned \"Monthly quota exceeded\", so I couldn't look up the docs as `CLAUDE.md` asks. I checked the API against the installed `openai` 3.19.2 source instead.\n- **`httpx2`, not `httpx`:** this SDK version is built on `httpx2`, so any stub transports need to be `httpx2` transports (for example `httpx2.MockTransport`).\n- **Leftover file:** my attempt to delete the scratch script `_check_client.py` in the project root was blocked by a permission prompt, so it's still there. Please delete it, or approve the removal and I'll do it."
  },
